      "class": "crypto_perp",
      "title": "crypto_perp class definition",
      "kind": "definition",
      "source": "seed: docs/refdata.md",
      "body": "# crypto_perp\n\nA perpetual futures contract on a cryptocurrency, quoted and settled in USDT,\nwith no expiry. Funding payments exchange hands between longs and shorts to\nanchor the mark price to spot.\n\nRegistry conventions for this class:\n\n- `id` shape: `crypto_perp:<venue>:<exchange_symbol>` in lowercase.\n- `venues` lists the venues where the contract trades; the seeded venue\n  `binance_usdt_m` is inferred from the trading bots' USDT-M style notionals\n  and fills, and must be confirmed against venue configuration before\n  position-limit logic relies on it.\n- `limits` keys (populated as they become known): `tick_size`, `lot_size`,\n  `min_notional`, `max_leverage`, `max_position`.\n- `meta.source` on seeded records names where the symbol was observed.\n"
    }
  ],
